SUMMARY:Dialogues on Democratic Resilience: 'Constitutional Courts in Times
  of Crisis: The Mexican Experience'
LOCATION:Online webinar
URL:https://www.law.cam.ac.uk/press/events/2026/11/dialogues-democratic-res
 ilience-constitutional-courts-times-crisis-mexican-experience
CATEGORIES:Law,Politics
DESCRIPTION:Faculty of Law\nHighlight: Senior figure speaking (Justice of t
 he Supreme Court)\nTopics: Law\, Politics\nDetails: https://www.law.cam.ac
 .uk/press/events/2026/11/dialogues-democratic-resilience-constitutional-co
 urts-times-crisis-mexican-experience\nSign-up needed: https://cam-ac-uk.zo
 om.us/webinar/register/WN_C3zFlTtARXqRjWSJ8Cm5BQ#/registration\nDate/time:
  \n\n Monday 23 November 2026 \n\n 5:00pm to 6:00pm\n\n Location: \n\n Onl
 ine webinar\n\n About \n\n Speakers: Alfredo Gutiérrez Ortiz Mena (Former
  Justice of the Supreme Court of Mexico and former Henry J. Steiner Lectur
 er in Human Rights at Harvard Law School)\n About the series: the Dialogue
 s on Democratic Resilience series provides a platform for scholars\, stude
 nts\, and members of the general public to examine the causes and dynamics
  of democratic decline and to explore strategies for strengthening democra
 tic institutions. Interdisciplinary in scope\, the series places particula
 r emphasis on the role of law and legal institutions\, investigating how t
 hey can both contribute to democratic erosion and function as vital safegu
 ards against.\n For questions\, please contact Dr Raffael Fasel ( rnf22@ca
 m.ac.uk )\n Register now
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:dept-www-law-cam-ac-uk-press-events-2026-11-3vbs-university-cambridge-e
 vent@cambridge-events
DTSTAMP:20261119T172102Z
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20261126T170000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20261126T180000
SUMMARY:3VB’s University of Cambridge Event
LOCATION:Downing College\, West Lodge & Maitland Room
URL:https://www.law.cam.ac.uk/press/events/2026/11/3vbs-university-cambridg
 e-event
CATEGORIES:Law,International
DESCRIPTION:Faculty of Law\nHighlight: Senior figure speaking (KC)\nTopics:
  Law\, International\nDetails: https://www.law.cam.ac.uk/press/events/2026
 /11/3vbs-university-cambridge-event\nSign-up needed\nDate/time: \n\n Thurs
 day 26 November 2026 \n\n 5:00pm to 6:00pm\n\n Location: \n\n Downing Coll
 ege\, West Lodge & Maitland Room\n\n About \n\n Following a brief introduc
 tion by 3VB's Rajesh Pillai KC\, members of 3VB will offer first-hand insi
 ghts into two recent landmark cases\, exploring how legal decisions are re
 ached and the role of barristers in shaping them.\n Dominic Kennelly will 
 discuss Spain v Infrastructure Services Luxembourg [2026] UKSC 9\, concern
 ing state immunity and the enforcement of international arbitration awards
 \, while William Day and Amelia-Rose Edwards will explore Gatwick Investme
 nt Ltd v Liberty Mutual Insurance Europe SE [2026] UKSC 14\, addressing co
 ntractual interpretation and causation in private law.\n The talks will be
  followed by drinks\, refreshments and an opportunity to network with memb
 ers of Chambers.\n RSVP: events@3vb.com
END:VEVENT
